<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia's May oil output average 630,000 bpd.</title>
<headline>Colombia's May oil output average 630,000 bpd.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia produced a daily average of 630,000 barrels of crude oil in May, state oil company Ecopetrol said.</p>
<p>It said the output figure was along the same lines seen in April and noted that foreign companies operating under association contracts with Ecopetrol were responsible for the bulk of production, with a total of 512,000 barrels per day.</p>
<p>The Cusiana field operated by British Petroleum in Colombia's eastern plains produced a daily average of 185,000 barrles of crude in May while the Cano Limon field operated by Occidental Petroleum saw daily output of 176,000 barrels, Ecopetrol said.</p>
<p>((-- Tom Brown, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
